<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) (Homo sapiens (soft-tissue mid-sagittal facial profile, 9 Wikimedia Commons photographs, 4 accepted))",
        "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens (soft-tissue mid-sagittal facial profile, 9 Wikimedia Commons photographs, 4 accepted) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-040-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens (soft-tissue mid-sagittal facial profile, 9 Wikimedia Commons photographs, 4 accepted) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens (soft-tissue mid-sagittal facial profile, 9 Wikimedia Commons photographs, 4 accepted)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: anything about populations or 'types'",
        "does_not_claim: growth or developmental mechanism",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 12 ordered pairs of 4 accepted photographs, landmark-only and dense (30 semilandmarks) configurations, LOO-CV, noise floor, controls",
        "reconstructed_in_script: E1 stretch, E3 shear with k = -cot(omega), E4 affine, E5 tan(phi') = tan(phi) + k; Dürer sub-family fit (5 dof) in the Camper frame vs scale+shift null and affine bound",
        "reported_in_source: Camper's facial angle 'is the index to a general deformation' (p. 742 footnote); no measurements in the source",
        "reported_in_source: Dürer heads redrawn in rectangular (Fig. 364) and oblique (Fig. 366) nets; Hough digitisation of the pinned scan gives omega = 81 / 99 deg, i.e. |k| ~ 0.15",
        "transfer_boundary: 2-D soft-tissue silhouettes from photographs, not skulls or 3-D form; Commons photographs are an analogue of Camper's drawn series and are labelled as such",
        "transfer_boundary: the Camper horizontal is approximated by the photograph horizontal after a declared deskew; +/-5 deg pose perturbation moves median R_Dürer 0.45 -> 0.37-0.40" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py; output: docs/media/t1917_040_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens (soft-tissue mid-sagittal facial profile, 9 Wikimedia Commons photographs, 4 accepted); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Dürer heads redrawn in rectangular (Fig. 364) and oblique (Fig. 366) nets; Hough digitisation of the pinned scan gives omega = 81 / 99 deg, i.e. |k| ~ 0.15 | Camper's facial angle 'is the index to a general deformation' (p. 742 footnote); no measurements in the source; reconstructed_in_script: E1 stretch, E3 shear with k = -cot(omega), E4 affine, E5 tan(phi') = tan(phi) + k; Dürer sub-family fit (5 dof) in the Camper frame vs scale+shift null and affine bound | 12 ordered pairs of 4 accepted photographs, landmark-only and dense (30 semilandmarks) configurations, LOO-CV, noise floor, controls; transfer_boundary: 2-D soft-tissue silhouettes from photographs, not skulls or 3-D form; Commons photographs are an analogue of Camper's drawn series and are labelled as such | the Camper horizontal is approximated by the photograph horizontal after a declared deskew; +/-5 deg pose perturbation moves median R_Dürer 0.45 -> 0.37-0.40; does_not_claim: anything about populations or 'types' | growth or developmental mechanism]; other sources: On Growth and Form <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Vier Bücher von menschlicher Proportion <https://archive.org/details/hierinnsindbegri00dure>, Soft tissue cephalometric analysis for orthognathic surgery <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6932485/>; phenomenon_size: 979 µm (0.0009792 m, log10=-3.009 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (20 runs from 979 µm to 2.85 m): 979 µm:cortical-sulcal-axon-tension, 1.4 mm:bressloff-cowan-V1-hallucination, 1.5 mm:corticothalamic-seizure-spirals, 1.7 mm:homo-sapiens-bioelectric-polarity, 3.1 mm:vertex-glass-jamming, 3.4 mm:homo-sapiens-vertex-packing, 6.3 cm:homo-sapiens-turing-wavelength, 11.7 cm:homo-sapiens-clock-wavefront" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0002-9416(68)90278-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1746-160X-10-54>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.0zpc86746> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-parameter-expressivity>,
