<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) — Code-to-model traceability: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring maps R2-R8 to functions; every transformation function cites its equation id and Thompson page; fit_durer's docstring derives c and k from U and states the Camper-frame rationale; the KG yaml links law -> Lean theorem -> code lines. Deductions: landmark-detection thresholds remain heuristic; the KG code loci point at Pass-1 line ranges that shifted in Pass 2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L528–L611: detect_landmarks heuristics (2 % / 0.3 % prominence, 2x li rule) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/22ee087d/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L528-L611>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The fitted family is now exactly Thompson's: a vertical scale, his horizontal stretch x' = c x (p. 730) and his oblique-net shear, in a frame fixed by a Camper horizontal, with the identifiability argument (shear vs rotation on collinear points) stated and tested by the pose-sensitivity check; the unconstrained affine is only an upper bound. The positive control recovers an exact grid to machine precision and the Lean theorems are mirrored one-to-one. Deductions: E2 logarithmic stretch still not implemented; the Camper horizontal is a photographic proxy, not porion-subnasale." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L119–L147: E2 (y -> eps^y) absent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/22ee087d/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L119-L147>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Residuals for null / similarity / Dürer / affine on landmark-only and dense configurations, LOO-CV for each family, a re-detection noise floor, KS test, CV of R, pose sensitivity, E5 regression (r, slope, p, RMSE) and three controls are all computed on real specimens and the verdict rule is written down before being applied. Deductions: n = 4 faces / 12 non-independent ordered pairs; the noise floor is a re-detection repeatability (lower bound of true landmark uncertainty); nasolabial SD 39 deg and convexity n = 2 mean the norm comparison is weak; LOO-CV shows the Dürer family does not generalise better than the null on this sample." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
